   "short_name": "FSSP",
   "long_name": "Forward Scattering Spectrometer Probe",
   "notes_public": "Rudolf Pueschel was the previous PI of FSSP.",
   "description": "The Forward Scattering Spectrometer Probe (FSSP) is an in situ airborne optical particle counter developed by Particle Measuring Systems, Inc. It measures particle size distribution by detecting the light intensity scattered by individual particles within a cloud. The FSSP detects particles ranging from 0.5 to 47 \u03bcm in diameter. It operates at a wavelength of 633 nm and typically samples at a rate of 1 Hz.",
