   "short_name": "2D-C/P",
   "long_name": "2D-C/P Hydrometeor Imaging Probe",
   "notes_public": "",
   "description": "The 2D-C/P Hydrometeor Imaging Probe is an in situ, airborne instrument that captures images of hydrometeors. It records these images by detecting the illuminated or shadowed states of the photodiode array as the hydrometeors' shadows pass over it. The 2D-C/P also provides measurements of particle size distribution, cloud droplet concentration, and hydrometeor shape. Typically, 2D-C/P probes have an image resolution of 25 micrometers and can image hydrometeors with diameters up to 1600 micrometers.",
